<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  The hardened-runtime entitlements of the signed bundle (scripts/macos/lib.sh
  signs with `- -options runtime` and this file, for the app of this Mac and
  for the release alike; docs/contributing/release.md §The macOS application). One entitlement, for the one thing the app does that the
  hardened runtime would otherwise refuse:

  - com.apple.security.device.audio-input — the microphone, for voice mode,
    asked for by `src/permissions.rs` with the usage description in Info.plist
    and only after the person turns the switch on in Settings › System.

  Nothing else is here on purpose. WKWebView runs its JIT out of process, so no
  allow-jit or allow-unsigned-executable-memory; the app loads only system
  frameworks, so no disable-library-validation; it sends no Apple Events; it
  is not sandboxed, so the network and file entitlements do not apply. The
  node inside the bundle (`Contents/MacOS/bisa`) is signed with the hardened
  runtime and no entitlements: it spawns processes and speaks on the loopback,
  which the runtime allows as it is.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
